WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.950
Step five collects the second
week, as of November sixteenth.

2
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:05.488
Still four notices.

3
00:00:05.488 --> 00:00:10.176
But chain example one, the maintenance,
now runs on November twenty-ninth,

4
00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.520
from four to eight in the morning, U T C.

5
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:17.600
Oracle rescheduled it, and the chain's
latest announcement replaced the first.

6
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.580
It's one notice with the new
window, so Module 7 updates its task

7
00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:25.950
instead of opening a second one, and
nobody prepares for the old date.

8
00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:29.562
Step six builds the live list
command without running it.

9
00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:34.308
It's Oracle's own list command for
the fictional tenancy, with all pages,

10
00:00:34.308 --> 00:00:39.300
only the latest in each chain, the region
from the settings, and J SON output.

11
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.787
A reviewer can see exactly what would run.

12
00:00:41.787 --> 00:00:46.313
Step seven runs this chapter's
tests: nine pass, none fail.

13
00:00:46.313 --> 00:00:48.220
Then delete the output folder.
